WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:09.040
In February 2022,
Beijing will host the Winter Olympics.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.480
The Chinese Communist Party will use
those games as a grand propaganda

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.280
spectacle to boost its domestic
legitimacy

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.039
and to boast of China's inexorable rise
on the international scene...

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:23.600
or so Xi Jinping hopes. Given the ongoing
human rights abuses in China, the Party's

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.920
culpability for the COVID-19 pandemic,
and its obvious inability to guarantee

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.240
the safety and well-being of Olympic
athletes,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.280
an international effort to move, cancel,
or boycott the Beijing games is in order.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.120
The 2022 Winter Olympic Games will take
place just months before the 20th

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.600
National Congress of the Chinese
Communist Party.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.360
A cancellation or significant boycott of
the Olympics might further weaken Xi

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.920
Jinping
in ways that make a leadership challenge,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.160
however remote that possibility,
somewhat more likely. Even if a boycott

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.280
or cancellation fails to put significant
pressure on Xi,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.960
absenting ourselves from the 2022 games
is the right thing to do.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.160
The alternative is to send team USA to
Beijing, and

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.040
in so doing, choose complicity in China's
worst abuses.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.439
Do you think the United States should
boycott the 2022 Winter Olympics?

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:14.880
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.479
scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to like and subscribe for

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.119
more research and videos from AEI.

